<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Husam al-Din Choban</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Çoban Bey</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Husam al-Din Choban was a commander of the Seljuk <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultanate-of-rum">Sultanate of Rum</a> who received the frontier district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kastamonu">Kastamonu</a> in the early 13th century. Around 1220 he led the Seljuk naval expedition across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudak">Sudak</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a>. He founded the Chobanid dynasty, which ruled Kastamonu until the 1290s.</p></div>
